ar 27 points and all seven race raters place this in the Solid or Safe Democratic column; markets price him at 98 to 99 percent.", "watch": "A major national backlash against Democrats or an unexpected scandal could narrow the race, but Cox would need a historic swing in a deeply blue state.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["Incumbent Wes Moore (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Governor Wes Moore, a Democrat, seeks a second term against Republican Dan Cox in a rematch of their 2022 contest. Maryland leans 15 points Democratic, and Moore holds an overwhelming financial edge, raising about $15.5 million to Cox's roughly $240,000, with $6.5 million still on hand. Every major race rater places the contest in the Solid or Safe Democratic column.\n\nRecent polls show Moore ahead by about 27 points among likely voters, and betting markets put his win chances near 98 to 99 percent. The two met in an early-October debate covering taxes, energy costs, and the economy, with no sign the race has narrowed. Cox would need a historic shift in a deeply blue state to threaten Moore's standing.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.996, "margin": 19.52}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9967, "margin": 19.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.998, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9939, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9968, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9958, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9956, "margin": 19.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9959, "margin": 19.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9942, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9961, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9947, "margin": 20.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9966, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9972, "margin": 23.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.994, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9986, "margin": 23.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.9974,